    "body": "Fixes #42208\n\n## Problem\n\n`remote#define#request()` increments `s:busy[chan]` before `rpcrequest()` and\ndecrements it afterwards. If `rpcrequest()` throws (the remote plugin raised an\nerror), the decrement is skipped. The channel stays busy and every later\n`remote#define#notify()` on it is queued forever.\n\n## Solution\n\nRelease the count and flush pending notifications in a `finally` block. The\nerror still propagates to the caller.\n\nTest: `remote#define#request does not block later notifications when the request fails`\n(fails on master, passes with this change).\n",
